      "user_input": ":role",
      "confidence": "Medium",
      "note": "False positive. Brakeman flags :role from its default dangerous-key list, but choosing the role is the purpose of the invite endpoint and MembershipPolicy#create? already limits it to active school staff of the current school. It is not a path to the privileged tier: User#backoffice? requires role 'backoffice' AND school_id nil AND an active membership, while People::CreateMembershipService builds through school.memberships (school_id is always the current school, never nil) and hardcodes status 'invited'. Role values are further constrained by Membership::ROLES. The :guardian_id key in the same permit list is dead - memberships has no guardian_id column and the service never reads it - and should be dropped, but that is a cleanup, not a vulnerability."
    }
  ],
  "brakeman_version": "8.0.5"
